# Whitelist approach: ignore everything by default, then explicitly
# un-ignore known source/asset file types. Compiled binaries produced by
# the per-example Makefiles have no extension (name == Makefile's TARGET),
# so this keeps them out of git without having to list every binary name.
*
!*/

!.gitignore
!Makefile*
!*.cu
!*.cuh
!*.h
!*.hpp
!*.cpp
!*.py
!*.md
!*.json
!*.ref
!*.png
!*.jpg
!*.jpeg
!*.raw
